{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/148067-changeling-slang","id":148067,"title":"Changeling Slang","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-24T13:03:27-07:00","id":148067,"title":"Changeling Slang","content":"Does anyone here remember the thread about changeling slang on the old forum? It turned up some pretty good stuff, as I recall. Any ideas about changeling-specific slang terms? Old-fashioned terms that have remained in use amongst changelings but fallen out of favour with everyone else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1664-thornfield13713","name":"Thornfield13713","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T14:23:02-07:00","id":148131,"title":"","content":"I do; there were some cool ones. The ones of mine I remember:<br /> <br /> Happily ever after: Marrying for material gain; can also be used in the form of X is looking for her happily ever after.<br /> <br /> The Chills: When an Autumn Courter takes their fear harvesting too far.<br /> <br /> Once upon a time: &quot;I fucked up&quot; - Once upon a time I brought some dodgy fate a goblin market.<br /> <br /> Stepford: A Spring Courter who's denying some obvious issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T16:18:30-07:00","id":148208,"title":"","content":"That really was a cool thread. Glad to see it coming back here.<br /> <br /> Also, you're in luck! You can still read the entire old-forum <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default6e5e.html?g=posts&amp;t=61368\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling Slang and Dialect thread</a>. It looks like Changeling the Lost fared much better than Exalted in the <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">White Wolf Forum Archive</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T17:58:20-07:00","id":149877,"title":"","content":"Edit: just read Gaius' post. Now I just feel seelie.<br /> <br /> I saved some of it, not all, but still. :3<br /> <br /> <b>Anger Management</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - A meeting of the Summer Court. &quot;They are having anger management meeting at the mill.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Bane</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - A weakness, a fault; a specific weakness tied to a changeling, a pledge or anything fae-related; the enemy or antagonist in a changeling's life (Gentry are known as &quot;The Greater Banes&quot; for this reason); a hunter who is hostile towards, or outright genocidal in regards to, changelings.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Boogie Man</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - A Title for the Autumn Courtier who's the most proficient in gathering fear. Usually reserved for one Changeling per freehold. &quot;I think the Boogie man visited the Orphanage last night.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Carnivalized</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - to be driven utterly crapsack insane by the Gentry, a fae pledge, bedlam, or anything fae-related; to be of very low Clarity; to incite chaos, usually through the use of the Fleeting Season contracts (as well as Verdant Spring), Bedlam, the Moon or the Vainglory contract, or various goblin contracts. Reckless Spring courtiers are often accused of doing this</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Chills, the</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - fear, but specifically fear intentionally farmed by the Autumn Court which is almost but not quite crossing the line into outright immorality. Almost a polite warning that they might think about toning it down a little. &quot;The Leaden Mirror have really been spreading the chills, using their contracts to make people believe they only just escaped from a serial killer.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Cob-gobbler</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - A derogatory term for a particularly promiscuous female (or male) Autumn courtier. &quot;Careful when dealing with her man, that chick's a major Cob-gobbler.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Cottager</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - someone who's laying low</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Dandy Ketch</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - an older and sarcastic way to refer to a person who puts up a respectable front but does unsavory things. Often used in an accusatory fashion or as a demeaning note, some of the younger generation changelings occasionally use it as a positive and even a trend defintion in some freeholds.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Daisyhead</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - derogatory name for a Spring Courtier</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Debate, a</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - when higher nobles fight. It sees mixed use between both younger and elder courtiers. Some of the former use it in a derogatory way and still others use it as a complement. It's all in the context. The same goes for how elders use it. Some see it easily as a compliment to seeing the nobles fighting as 'more refined and elegant' and others are dismissive of the term altogether.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Dustmop</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - a butt-kisser, someone who the Nobles walk all over, a particularly pathetic or snivelling Loyalist.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Flippin' a Deal</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - making a Pledge. &quot;Right, why don't we flip a deal here?&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Frostbite</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - A threat used by Winter courtiers to keep other Changelings from getting in their business</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">&quot;I think you'd best stay outta our part of town, you don't want to catch frostbite.&quot; </span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Gingerbread</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - Something dangerous or deceptive; a trick or trap; something too good to be true.&quot;This whole job smells like gingerbread, to me.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Glaze</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - another term for Glamour. &quot;I'm feel'n grayed out, man. Gotta get glazed soon&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Glut</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - derogatory name for a gristlegrinder ogre</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Grayed Out</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - when a changeling is out of glamour</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Hedgefresh</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - a recent escapee from Arcadia</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Hob</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - a hob goblin</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Hob-conned</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - when a Hob &quot;twists&quot; the truth about a product in a Goblin Market. Usually in the context of a purchase. &quot;Ol' John got hob conned when he bought that Token!&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Ironside</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - The mortal world, so named because of the abundance of metal/steel</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Keeper's Pet</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - a loyalist.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Meditatin</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - (Usually) A fairest getting laid with a mortal, generally a one night stand for the glamour.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">&quot;Where is he? Oh, he left with a blonde to do some meditatin. Said he wants to be ready to impress the crowd during his 'debate' tomorrow.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Nemo</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - a fetch</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Norm</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - a normal human; someone not supernatural</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Pathboy/Pathgirl</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - Someone who compulsively follows faerie tale rules like &quot;don't leave the path&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Redcap</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - a Summer Courtier</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Riding Hood</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - Setting a trap by sending someone in as bait, with the calvelry coming in not long after. Often used to try and get info from the targets before pounding their face into the curp. Bait is usually reffered to as 'Red'. Sometimes used in a different manner by following the 'Red' to a meet then busting it up after it starts. This has lead to some misunderstandings. &quot;I swear, I didn't know they wee following me! Yeah I know they said they was riding my hood, but I swear I wasn't in on it...&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Rossetti</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - a changeling who has been fully accepted as a goblin merchant. Named after the author of the poem &quot;Goblin Market&quot;.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Snowfall</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - A winter court operation. Usually implied to be cloak and dagger stuff.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">&quot;Better keep your head down tonight, I hear a snowfall is coming.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Snowflake</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - a derogatory term for a Winter courtier.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Spring break</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> When a spring courtier breaks someone by manipulating his/her desires. This is used when done deliberately.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Spook</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - an Autumn courtier.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Spookshow</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - a group of Autumn Courtiers</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Spookshow Baby</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - a somewhat derogatory way to refer to an attractive Autumn courtier</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Stepford</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - a Spring Courter who's clearly faking the being happy or otherwise unscared by Arcadia; a Fairest who's overly reliant on mortal approval, especially approval outside of genuine friendship, for their emotional heath. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Tousler</b><span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> - a spiteful name for a guard. Used to show annoyance at one such as a bouncer throwing one out or a Noble Guard not letting one in to see the noble.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T22:22:21-07:00","id":150037,"title":"","content":"Hey, happens to the best of us. Probably good to winnow out some &quot;Best of&quot; outta the giant old thread, anyway. And hey, bright side:<br /> <br /> <b>Feeling Seelie</b> - Describes a flight of fancy or a whimsical state of mind, inclination, or perspective (sometimes foolish, especially over something post hoc), and typically not for a matter seen as serious. &quot;Okay, my little one-liner wasn't the height of professionalism, let it go; I'd knocked back some glamour and I was feelin' seelie.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T17:20:15-07:00","id":150905,"title":"","content":"That thread was awesome. Particularly proud of Tousler and a Debate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T13:42:20-07:00","id":154154,"title":"","content":"<b>Poison Apple</b>: Something that's obviously a trap, but which someone might be unable to avoid.<br /> <br /> &quot;It was a total poison apple -- I couldn't say no to the deal with the King right there!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Glass Slipper:</b> A particular talent or quirk that is unique to an individual. A tell. Variations include glass heels and glass shoes in general.<br /> <br /> &quot;It's just his glass slipper -- he's always gotta turn things upside down when no one's looking.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;If you need someone discreetly out of the picture, the winter court's got a shoebox of glass slippers for you.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Bluebeard:</b> Someone known for seducing and using people, especially betraying people in committed relationships. Alternatively, a sexual predator, depending on the needs for the game.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T19:50:31-07:00","id":157325,"title":"","content":"If it's okay, I have some of my own Changeling slang-- I wasn't on the old forum....<br /> <br /> <b>Leaves in your hair:</b> someone who has recently escaped the Gentry and Hedge<br /> &quot;You haven't visited Court yet? I didn't realize that you still had leaves in your hair... you need to get a patron quick&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit-Touched, Lost, Betwixt</b>: Changelings and Hobs of all sorts<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Eaters</b>: Fetches<br /> <br /> <b>Broken Ones</b>: Werewolves, Vampires (in my campaign, all non-humans are fey, the unusual characteristics of those creatures are a result of Oathbreaking with Contracts).<br /> <br /> <b>Neverwhere, Underland, Wonderland:</b> Arcadia<br /> <br /> <b>Edge, Maze, Frontier</b>: Hedge<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2002-quynce","name":"Quynce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2002_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T15:56:24-07:00","id":161998,"title":"","content":"I like &quot;Shadow Eaters&quot; -- very creepy and pretty thematic :3a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T17:58:30-07:00","id":163019,"title":"","content":"I would like to suggest &quot;Spinning Straw&quot; for when completing the Task portion of a Pledge. As in &quot;Mikey wanted to come today, but he's busy spinning straw for that goblin.&quot;<br /> Further adding into &quot;gold&quot; or &quot;dross&quot; would reflect how beneficial/pleasent or onerous/difficult the tasked individual may feel about their situation. &quot;Tomorrow I start to spin straw into gold for that norm that agreed to give me their penthouse for a month.&quot; or &quot;stealing that thing for a simple favor, was a real straw to dross deal.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T17:58:37-07:00","id":199479,"title":"","content":"The thing about slang is it's gotta roll off the tongue and be easy to throw into a conversation, almost as if by reflex. Follow that rule, and you're two thirds of the way done in making some good character slang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T12:00:34-07:00","id":201327,"title":"","content":"<b>Peter Pan:</b> A privateer who specializes in targeting children and convincing them to follow back to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mundane World:</b> Another word for the human world, referring to the diminished supply of magic that flows there in comparison to other realms (Such as Arcadia, or the supernal)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fairy Dust:</b> A comical term used to refer to the Glamour that one is using to power their Fae abilities. &quot;Man, I'm running a little low on Fairy Dust after that fight!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Baggins:</b> A term used to refer to someone who takes on suicide missions for the good of the Freeholds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Humpty Dumpty:</b> A derogatory term for someone who is accident prone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nymph:</b> Another term for a perverted or sex addicted female Fae. &quot;Oh man, that girl is a total Nymph!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Satyr:</b> The male equivalent to Nymph, referring to perverted or sex addicted male Fae. &quot;Hey, my eyes are up here, Satyr!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Warlord:</b> A derogatory term for a ruler of the Summer Court who prefers to resort to violence as their first response to a problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Red Queen:</b> Those who pass out harsh punishments for even the most minor of offenses. Often used to refer to the tyrannical ruler of whatever Court holds dominance in the Freeholds at the time. &quot;Don't step on the flower garden, it belongs to the Red Queen!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-18-2014, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T20:25:27-07:00","id":204606,"title":"","content":"<b>Tweedle:</b> A derogatory term for a pair of Lost with noticeably low intellect. &quot;Well if it isn't Tweedle Dee, and Tweedle Dum!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rumpelstiltskin: </b>The act of setting up a Pledge with a seemingly impossible loop hole (such as correctly telling the contractor their name even though they've never revealed it to you). &quot;I think that Hob pulled a Rumpelstiltskin on me!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Deal's Off:</b> The act of legally breaking a Pledge without suffering the consequences that would normally be imposed for doing so. &quot;Alright, the deal's off!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cthulhu:</b> A comical term for members of the True Fae. &quot;Oh shit, here comes Cthulhu!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Evil Twin: </b>A comical term for someone's Fetch. &quot;That's not me, it's my evil twin!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>LARPing:</b> The act of conducting Fae related business in public (i.e around non-Changelings) &quot;Don't mind us folks, we're just LARPing!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T14:39:27-07:00","id":210581,"title":"","content":"Late to the party, but its good to be back <br /> I remember mine and a few others. <br /> <br /> <br /> Hob conned: When a hobgoblin &quot;twists&quot; the truth, usually in regards to a Token. <br /> &quot;Ol John got hob conned on that one! &quot;<br /> <br /> Flippin' a deal: Making a Pledge.<br /> &quot;Right, lets flip a deal.&quot;<br /> <br /> Spookshow: Derogatory term for an Autumn court member.<br /> <br /> Spookshow baby: Derogatory term for an attractive frmale Autumn courtier. <br /> <br /> <br /> Last two weren't mine, hope I got them right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3577-vechi","name":"vechi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T07:18:15-07:00","id":213520,"title":"","content":"<b>Alice</b> - A human (typically female) who accidentally wanders into The Hedge or Arcadia.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hatter</b> - A term for unusually helpful Mad, who seem more interested in making friends than slicing your eyes out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cheshire</b> - A derogatory nickname for someone who takes on the role of being an adviser / guide, but always flees at the first sign of trouble. Only to return once the danger has passed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Absalom</b> - A derogatory nickname for someone who possesses vast knowledge and wisdom, but treats everyone as inferior because of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fairy</b> - A term used to refer to a Changeling who insists on adhering human interpretations of their Kiths / Seemings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T04:04:12-08:00","id":312128,"title":"","content":"A couple that have turned up in my games:<br /> <br /> <b>Winter Break</b>: When a winter courtier is doing something the court wouldn't approve of or doesn't match the court stereotype. &quot;Did you see Silas partying up with those frat boys? I guess he's on winter break.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Poor Life Choices</b>: A term for a changeling who has to keep being rescued by their motley mates or their court, usually in sympathy for those who have to keep up with the rescuing.. &quot;Did you hear that they had to rescue Adrian again? Man, Poor Life Choices.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T08:46:06-08:00","id":318284,"title":"","content":"Beat thread ever. I just wish had any ideas to add<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","name":"Nurseninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T11:02:01-08:00","id":320896,"title":"","content":"<b>Fae-holes</b>- Privateers and loyalist that mingle with changelings and Humans a like, just to kidnap or deceive them. &quot; Can't believe those guys did that... Bunch of Fae-holes. &quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Down the Rabbit Hole</b>- Oneiromancers term for dream diving or travel.<br /> <br /> <b>Now Make a wish</b>- What a changeling says to seal a contract or a pledge. A terming meaning. &quot;Hope for the best.&quot; after there agreement is settled, usually through handshake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T11:30:33-08:00","id":320907,"title":"","content":"CLOCKING IN- Where a Court gives up its power.<br /> <br /> OVER THE GARDEN WALL- A part of the Hedge know for being relatively non-hostile. <br /> <br /> BEATRICE/VIRGIL- A Hedge-guide who works for little to no pay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T11:51:32-08:00","id":320960,"title":"","content":"<b>Highlander:</b> A Changeling who slays their Fetch. &quot;Man, she just went Highlander on that Fetch yesterday!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Toll Troll:</b> A bouncer, guard, or watchman who can be bribed to allow access.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tinkerbell:</b> A derogatory term for a guide or legal guardian who is disrespected by their wards.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Blind Mice:</b> A derogatory term for a Motley who constantly get into danger. &quot;Well if it isn't the 3 Blind Mice!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jester:</b> A term for deceptively cunning Changelings who hide their wit behind a display of stupidity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Frog Prince:</b> A term for an ugly male who craves intimate affection from beautiful women.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T01:33:07-07:00","id":439610,"title":"","content":"<b>Popsicle:</b> A derogatory term for Winter Court members. Often accompanied by a more colorful explanation for added insult.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You know why we call yer kind Popsicles, Herb? Cus yer all frosty as fuck and have sticks up your asses.&quot;</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>i don't know a hecking thing, my guy","edited":{"userid":4416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4416-heedra","user":"Heedra","date":". 03-13-2015, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4416-heedra","name":"Heedra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T12:24:04-07:00","id":440288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danparadox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/148067-changeling-slang?p=312128#post312128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Poor Life Choices</b>: A term for a changeling who has to keep being rescued by their motley mates or their court, usually in sympathy for those who have to keep up with the rescuing.. &quot;Did you hear that they had to rescue Adrian again? Man, Poor Life Choices.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In the spirit of the old thread, I absolutely love this one. Mainly because I immediately got an image of a changeling trying to explain it to this werewolf girl he's been going out with for a while, and then a few months later hearing a local pack he doesn't know that well using it in conversation. And then one of the local vampires almost gets staked, he hears it at the kindred-owned bar he's supposed to meet his new contact at. And then when he almost kills a hunter who tried to jump him until the rest of the hunter's cell shows up, as the changeling is stealthily following them to find out where their base is, they start cracking wise about poor life choices.<br /> <br /> It just fits EVERYWHERE, man!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/768-djehuty3","name":"djehuty3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T12:54:18-07:00","id":441750,"title":"","content":"<b>Sketchers: </b>Changelings who underwent painting, portrait, or other artwork-based Durance, and in consequence now resemble living artwork or craftwork.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T19:35:47-07:00","id":453664,"title":"","content":"<b>Fit to Trim:</b> Someone you think is better off dead, or whom you're planning to kill. &quot;That old codger is fit to trim, I think!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Hedgesold:</b> Creatures from the mortal world that got lost in the Hedge, and were captured, bought and traded for by the Gentry and Hobgoblins. &quot;That poor collie's probably hedgesold by now.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Golden Ticket:</b> A one-in-a-million chance to get out of a really bad bargain, oath or pledge. &quot;There's your golden ticket, NOW TAKE IT!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T22:28:55-07:00","id":453851,"title":"","content":"<b>Potter:</b> A mage who has frequent dealings with Lost or Fae<br /> <br /> <b>Juggernaut:</b> A derogatory term for Ogres with poor diplomacy skills. &quot;Well peace talks failed, send in the Juggernaut!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Super Hero / Heroine:</b> An eccentric Lost who dedicates their powers to upholding the laws of society.<br /> <br /> <b>Hermit:</b> A Lost who prefer to live on the other side of the Hedge, despite the dangers that dwell there.<br /> <br /> <b>Pet:</b> A derogatory term for those who voluntarily serve the True Fae. &quot;Run on back to your master like a good little pet!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Kruger:</b> A Lost who tortures people in their dreams for entertainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T07:47:05-07:00","id":454364,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>How about some school based slang?<br /> <br /> <br /> Prep Schooler:</b> A derogatory term for Changelings who are actively trying to become Gentry. &quot;When I see one of you damned prep schoolers, I just want to kick your teeth in!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Public Schooling:</b> A basic or learn-from-experience level of understanding the workings of Arcadia and The Hedge. &quot;Man, the public schooling system is pathetic these days!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hall Monitor:</b> A guardian who bars free passage in The Hedge.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Principal's Office:</b> The domain of a True Fae. &quot;I haven't heard from her since she got sent to the Principal's Office&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Drop Out:</b> A Changeling who attempts to abandon all ties to the Fae world, and live as a normal human.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Expelled:</b> A lost who is banished from stepping foot within Arcadia. &quot;What did you do to get expelled? Must have been pretty bad!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Teacher's Pet:</b> A Gentry's favorite Loyalist.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pre-Schooler:</b> A freshly captured mortal, not yet affected by the magic of Arcadia.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bully: </b>A derogatory term for a Lost who abuses their powers, especially targeting weaker victims.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Class, the: </b>The collective slaves gathered by a Gentry. &quot;Settle down now, class. We have much to do today!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Class Pet:</b> A Lost who's status is beneath that of most other slaves. &quot;Okay, now who's turn is it to feed the class pet?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clique:</b> Motley who share a common theme, style, hobby or personality traits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Substitute:</b> A Fetch<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Freshman:</b> A Lost who's Wyrd level is between 1 and 3<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sophmore:</b> A lost who's Wyrd level is between 4 and 6<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Junior:</b> A lost who's Wyrd level is between 7 and 9<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Senior:</b> A Lost's who's Wyrd level is 10 or possibly higher</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-12-2016, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T06:56:27-07:00","id":479020,"title":"","content":"LOL, oh man I can't believe my Cob-Gobbler line survived to make it here, that makes me happy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh, here is an old one that Sikla did based, that was actually inspired by me and a few others (Arcanewatcher, MrParaduo to be precise);<br /> <br /> <b>Oh you:</b> A subtle way of telling someone in your motley to shut up after they say something embarrassing; a term of endearment among Autumn courtiers, referring to how some find the scary stuff they say...endearing.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T15:50:44-07:00","id":479575,"title":"","content":"<b>Picasso:</b> A dual kith who possess the traits of two extremely different roles (i.e Corpsegrinder + Dancer, ).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beethoven:</b> A Lost who possesses a disability that contradicts their talents or skills. (i.e deaf musician, blind painter est).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nunchucks:</b> An amusing (though derogatory) term for a Summer Courtier who doesn't know how to fight. (i.e, flailing wildly in battle).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T18:50:06-07:00","id":480997,"title":"","content":"Love Conquers All: an admonishment, typically given after hearing an obvious lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T09:02:46-07:00","id":483582,"title":"","content":"Grim: A Changeling whose Durance seems remarkably similar to a well known fairy tale.<br /> <br /> Hollywood: A Changeling whose Durance that seems to have been inspired by more modern media.<br /> <br /> Cross Dresser: A Changeling who has abilities similar to those possessed by another kind of Supernatural Creature.<br /> <br /> Patchwork: A Motley whose members are so diverse that it seems unthinkable that they would ever associate with each other, let alone work together (aka your average group of PC's).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T16:30:46-07:00","id":487783,"title":"","content":"<b>Bombadil:</b> A mysterious, helpful being who's nature is unclear.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Voldemort:</b> A traitor who's betrayal nearly brought ruin to the Freehold.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Crocker: </b>A human that relentlessly tries to acquire proof of the existence of Fae. Possibly a Hunter with a narrow focus on prey.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Teddy:</b> A Beast who devotes themselves to protecting children from those who seek to harm them. The slang is sometimes followed by what kind of animal they represent (i.e Teddy Bear).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Freakazoid:</b> One of the Mad who still proves helpful to the Freehold... somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-01-2017, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T09:56:58-07:00","id":488391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/148067-changeling-slang?p=487783#post487783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Voldemort:</b> A traitor who's betrayal nearly brought ruin to the Freehold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't it be:<br /> <br /> Wormtail: A traitor who's betrayal nearly brought ruin to the Freehold.<br /> <br /> Voldemort: The Gentry that benefited from said betrayal. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T14:20:54-07:00","id":488713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/148067-changeling-slang?p=488391#post488391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shouldn't it be:<br /> <br /> Wormtail: A traitor who's betrayal nearly brought ruin to the Freehold.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't <b><i>that</i></b> be: Worm-tongue? And/or: Grimer? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T18:29:01-07:00","id":490108,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Keeper Of All: an alternative name for the Wyrd, as it can transform/control the lives of humans, changelings, True Fae and other monsters alike, subtly or not. May or may not be conflated with the Holy Spirit/Abrahamic God.<br /> <br /> Chess: a slang used by changelings and Ensorcelled to refer to the Feud of the Gentry in general. Sometimes the Gentry use this slang too.<br /> <br /> Chess Piece: someone manipulated in order to benefit a Feud. Sub-terms may include King and Queen for important agents and Pawns for minor ones. Who is the Gentry, then? The guy playing chess, of course.<br /> <br /> Sport: slang used mainly by the Gentry to refer to Feuds that are primarily physical in nature. Usually involves more pain than normal sports.<br /> <br /> Chat: slang used mainly by the Gentry to refer to Feuds that are primarily social in nature. Usually involves backstabbing that would make the average Kindred or Unchained proud.<br /> <br /> Puzzle: slang used mainly by Gentry to refer to Feuds that are primarily mental in nature. Usually involves something like a pendulum with an ax swinging ever closer to make the others think faster.<br /> <br /> Debate: an euphemism for when two or more Gentry are fighting over something, usually a slave or Title.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-23-2015, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T19:37:39-07:00","id":491182,"title":"","content":"<b>The Woodsman:</b> A slang term referring to a singular Hunter. &quot;And so the Woodsman took his ax and cleaved the wolf's stomach open. Freeing Red Riding Hood and her grandmother!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Japedo: </b>A Gentry who displays affection towards Elementals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Obstacle Course:</b> A particularly difficult pathway through the Hedge.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Poisoned Apple:</b> Popular among Loyalists and Gentry for capturing others. The Poisoned Apple is a glamour endowed fruit that produces narcotic effects in those who eat it. Such as rendering them unconscious!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T03:36:49-07:00","id":492486,"title":"","content":"<b>Bread-Crumbed</b>; Marked Territory or Sanctuary for the Freehold.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T20:34:16-07:00","id":517579,"title":"","content":"<b>Sir Robin:</b> One who frequently acts in direct opposition to their title, and then denies it publicly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Castle Anthrax:</b> A place of depravity which puts on a front of being virtuous and upstanding citizens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Tim, the Conjurer:</b> A wizard who uses their powers during unnecessary situations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Killer Rabbit:</b> A guard who disguises themselves as something innocent and harmless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T11:40:50-07:00","id":518338,"title":"","content":"<b>Magic Beans</b> - A shoddy product; a sham; snake oil. &quot;I once bought some discount hedgespun clothes at the Goblin Market. Turned out they were just magic beans.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Bean Seller</b> - One who sells magic beans (see above); a con artist. &quot;Don't tell me you actually believe this bean seller?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T12:12:57-07:00","id":518363,"title":"","content":"<b>Wearing Emerald Glasses</b> - gullible or easily fooled; percieving magical or Fae influence where none exists; occasionally used to describe Lost who have difficulty discerning fiction from reality due to Clarity loss. &quot;Take off the emerald glasses, Frank, it's just a coincidence.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T14:36:54-07:00","id":518436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/148067-changeling-slang?p=154154#post154154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Glass Slipper:</b> A particular talent or quirk that is unique to an individual. A tell. Variations include glass heels and glass shoes in general.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;It's just his glass slipper -- he's always gotta turn things upside down when no one's looking.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Specific to 2E, this would be a great way to refer to someone's Icon(s).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T17:30:56-07:00","id":518605,"title":"","content":"<b>Grail / Fox: </b>The current target of Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> <b>Questing Beast / Wolf:</b> A changeling or other individual who has managed to piss off a Huntsman personally, becoming the focus of their schemes.<br /> <br /> <b> Green Knight / Dragon: </b>The above, and they <i>revel </i>in it. Regarded as suicidally stupid by everyone who is not a Green Knight.<br /> <br /> <b>Red Herring: </b>Hewing to the original definition, a trap for Huntsmen. How a Dragon redeems their name.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T23:04:26-08:00","id":784567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/148067-changeling-slang?p=479575#post479575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Picasso:</b> A dual kith who possess the traits of two extremely different roles (i.e Corpsegrinder + Dancer, ).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Beethoven:</b> A Lost who possesses a disability that contradicts their talents or skills. (i.e deaf musician, blind painter est).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nunchucks:</b> An amusing (though derogatory) term for a Summer Courtier who doesn't know how to fight. (i.e, flailing wildly in battle).</div> </div> </div> </div>dude,a corpsegrinder plus dancer is exactly what i needed to make a badasss/surreal character,just imagine the changeligns keeper being like &quot;yeah,so i'm gonna need you chew on that dead tree's root or i'll have to go about to the mortal word and eviscerate your sister,oh and if you could do some brakedance while you were at it that'd be quit swell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T13:18:10-08:00","id":786888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shouldn't it be:<br /> <br /> Wormtail: A traitor who's betrayal nearly brought ruin to the Freehold.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't <b><i>that</i></b> be: Worm-tongue? And/or: Grimer? <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually these two together gives a good reason for this slang:<br /> <br /> <b>Can o' Worms: </b>Group of traitors and/or plot to bring ruin to the freehold.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I hate finding all these cans o' worms.&quot; </i>Jared sighs.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You'd hate not finding them more.&quot;</i> Pip retorts glibly.<br /> <br /> Jared.taps his cold iron spike and says with grim determination<br /> <i>&quot;Guess it's time to open up this can o' worms&quot;</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-15-2015, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T02:48:47-08:00","id":787244,"title":"","content":"<b>Steel Worker</b>: An unintentional saboteur; comes from mortals who smelted the precious cold iron that protect a freehold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T13:59:41-08:00","id":787616,"title":"","content":"<b>Little Mermaid</b>: A changeling who rejects all Freeholds and courts to try and recapture a mundane life, either their old one or an assumed one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T18:17:10-08:00","id":807483,"title":"","content":"<b>Chessmaster: </b>A gentry who is either using changelings in war, or one who is hunting a lost, and seems to be able to catch them anywhere.<br /> <i>&quot;The Gentry looking for Simon is a Chessmaster. I hope the poor bastard manages to find someplace safe.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10751-belac93","name":"Belac93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10751_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T19:30:16-08:00","id":807520,"title":"","content":"<b>Boogeyman:</b> A Huntsman who strikes at night and returns to Arcadia at sunrise.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sprite:</b> Lost who retain the personality of young children, especially known for their playful innocence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Neverland:</b> A Gentry's realm that seems attractive enough to take up residence!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T20:31:13-08:00","id":807558,"title":"","content":"<b>Arnie/Smith:</b> A Huntsman who's even more persistant than normal, especially if they end up getting fataly injured a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T12:01:22-07:00","id":1145861,"title":"","content":"Bit of a Necro: but I thought of one that is pretty nifty<br /> <br /> Kaulder: An Ensorcelled or formerly Ensorcelled human who now hunts down Changelings, often a Hunter but sometimes a dupe roped into the task by loyalists or Privateers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T13:03:55-07:00","id":1145875,"title":"","content":"Warlocker - Autumn Court member, Warlock, who insists that their membership in Court and pursuit of Arcane Secrets somehow makes them superior to others.<br /> Believed to derive its etymology from &quot;locker&quot;, alluding to stereotype of bullies showing nerds into lockers and suggesting it as punishment for offending Spook. Integrated into Autumn Court lexicon as well.<br /> Uses: &quot;Ease up, junior. Don't be such a warlocker.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user"